==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|sunnentac|sunne(n)tac}}, {{m|gmh|sunntac|sun(n)tac}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|sunnūntag}} (9th c.), from late {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*sunnōniz dagaz||day of the sun}}, a calque of Latin {{m|la|dies Solis}} (4th c.). Compare Low German {{m|nds|Sünndag}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zondag}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|snein}}, English {{m|en|Sunday}}, Danish {{m|da|søndag}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈzɔntaːk/|[ˈzɔntʰaˑkʰ]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Sonntag.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

